./claim/RetiredNumber.java:13:public class RetiredNumber {
/** A claim number a re-dated claim left behind as it moved to another period: never given again. */
/** While a user's screen shows a sheet as of a date, every request it makes carries that date in
 *  {@link #HEADER}: each read answers with the sheet as it stood at the end of that date, and every
 *  changing request is refused (403, the date echoed in {@link #HEADER}) before it reaches its
 *  handler, so it writes nothing; a handler
 *  marked {@link AsOfAllowed} changes nothing and is let through. */
    /** The header carrying the date (yyyy-mm-dd) the screen shows the sheet as of. */
        registry.addInterceptor(this).addPathPatterns("/api/sheets/**");
/**
 * The sheet's history: each version of its claims, people, rates, settings, periods, statements,
 * patrons, watches, roles and delegations a change left, with the sheet's today when the change was
 * made (one removed leaves an empty version). A version is written (by {@link HistoryListener}, in
 * the change's own transaction, so a refused change writes none) only when it differs from the one
 * before it. {@link #asOf} rebuilds the sheet as it stood at the end of a date.
 */

